WEBVTT

00:00.100 --> 00:04.310
<b>Late November, Unified Year 1926</b>

00:05.260 --> 00:06.910
Nothing but ammo.

00:06.910 --> 00:08.730
Not nearly enough stuff for daily life.

00:09.250 --> 00:12.250
I was hoping for some socks, at least.

00:12.250 --> 00:16.310
We work directly for Strategic HQ, 
and this is all we get.

00:16.310 --> 00:19.490
That tells you everything you need 
to know about the Eastern Front.

00:22.710 --> 00:24.500
What an awful sky.

01:56.550 --> 02:01.470
This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.

02:07.380 --> 02:09.780
Sorry I'm late.

02:13.780 --> 02:18.570
It's rare for you to invite me 
to go drinking, though.

02:19.040 --> 02:22.270
I actually found something interesting.

02:27.250 --> 02:28.800
Start it up.

02:38.210 --> 02:39.720
What a surprise.

02:39.720 --> 02:43.090
It reminds you of the days with 
Regiment Commander Laudon.

02:45.070 --> 02:48.560
Brings you right back to 
those days in hell, right?

02:48.560 --> 02:50.260
Yeah.

02:50.260 --> 02:52.550
I can feel my back soaking with sweat.

02:52.550 --> 02:55.560
It wasn't just used in place 
of a wake-up trumpet.

02:55.560 --> 02:58.530
It was for food, baths, even the toilet.

02:58.790 --> 03:00.950
I don't know how I made it through.

03:00.950 --> 03:03.820
I never would have without you there.

03:04.030 --> 03:06.330
That goes for both of us.

03:06.680 --> 03:08.880
I was told they stopped making these.

03:10.000 --> 03:12.870
I found it at a flea market.

03:12.870 --> 03:15.310
They didn't let it go for cheap, though.

03:15.310 --> 03:19.370
It's a small price for a chance 
to look back on those days.

03:19.870 --> 03:21.260
That's right.

03:21.690 --> 03:25.390
I'll leave it here. 
Come listen any time you want.

03:26.810 --> 03:28.730
I think I'll do just that.

03:29.390 --> 03:33.400
<b>Episode Two:
A Strange Friendship</b>

03:34.820 --> 03:37.790
It's been over 30 years, huh?

03:37.790 --> 03:40.840
Time does fly, doesn't it?

03:40.840 --> 03:42.300
Sure does.

03:44.780 --> 03:49.630
But we don't have time to 
reminisce upon the good old days.

03:49.630 --> 03:51.040
That's right.

03:53.130 --> 03:56.570
Zettour, you and I have 
known each other for eons.

03:56.570 --> 04:00.800
As an old friend, I want you to 
give me your honest opinion.

04:02.280 --> 04:04.540
Winter came too soon.

04:05.110 --> 04:09.270
Quickly eliminating the enemy's 
field army is impossible now.

04:09.270 --> 04:11.550
We should rebuild our lines.

04:12.440 --> 04:17.660
So we have to be prepared for 
insults from the incompetent, huh?

04:18.390 --> 04:20.510
The problem is what happens 
when spring arrives.

04:20.510 --> 04:23.330
Are we assuming
 we'll resume the offensive?

04:23.600 --> 04:25.820
It's the only way forward.

04:27.020 --> 04:31.320
The Empire is just barely managing 
to keep itself supplied.

04:31.650 --> 04:36.040
And that's assuming
 it uses every possible resource.

04:37.490 --> 04:40.840
Blood continues to flow, even now.

04:42.600 --> 04:43.850
And yet...

04:44.570 --> 04:49.370
Our future is not totally hopeless yet.

04:50.140 --> 04:53.600
<b>Allied Kingdom Capital: Londinium</b>

04:53.840 --> 04:57.790
Now, how's our new friend, 
the devil, working?

04:57.790 --> 05:01.320
Ideally, they and the Empire 
slaughter each other.

05:01.320 --> 05:04.120
The Federation is... struggling.

05:04.120 --> 05:07.940
They'll be bringing back the mages 
that they purged, it seems,

05:07.940 --> 05:11.280
but they won't be able to take 
advantage of numerical superiority.

05:11.280 --> 05:12.370
And so...

05:12.370 --> 05:15.560
Let's use that volunteer army.

05:15.870 --> 05:18.780
We'll be able to make it look like 
we're working with the Federation,

05:18.780 --> 05:23.140
while getting the same intelligence
we would if we were spying on them.

05:23.130 --> 05:26.050
<b>Federation Capital: Moskva</b>

05:24.160 --> 05:26.060
Are you sure about this?

05:26.060 --> 05:27.550
Of course.

05:27.550 --> 05:31.790
Sending forces to the volunteer army 
is just what we need.

05:31.790 --> 05:34.350
I'd rather have the Allied Kingdom

05:34.350 --> 05:37.340
working for us as an ally 
than being our enemy.

05:37.340 --> 05:39.680
We'll need a propaganda 
strategy from now on.

05:40.750 --> 05:46.460
Thankfully, we're at war with the Empire, 
the collective enemy of the world.

05:46.460 --> 05:49.940
We need to show everyone that 
the Federation are the good guys.

05:50.470 --> 05:52.740
So we'll pick someone 
appropriate for the task.

05:52.740 --> 05:57.080
Yes. Someone loyal to the party, 
and idealistic, should be in charge.

05:57.480 --> 06:01.070
And someone charismatic 
should be the mage.

06:01.070 --> 06:02.080
Understood.

06:06.320 --> 06:08.050
Of course, right?

06:08.050 --> 06:13.300
That's the army that saw the fairy!

06:13.300 --> 06:16.040
Don't worry, I'll catch you soon!

06:18.730 --> 06:23.520
Jeez... the brass are pushing 
dealing with their friends onto us.

06:20.190 --> 06:23.520
<b>Multinational Volunteer Army Battalion Leader (Allied Kingdom Citizen)
Lt. Colonel William Douglas Drake</b>

06:33.430 --> 06:35.450
I apologize for keeping you waiting.

06:35.450 --> 06:40.040
<b>Federation Political Commissar Attached to the Multinational Volunteer Army
Lt. Liliya Ivanovna Tanechka</b>

06:35.820 --> 06:38.840
I am Liliya Ivanovna Tanechka.

06:38.840 --> 06:42.000
This is Colonel Mikel, a Federation mage.

06:40.040 --> 06:42.960
<b>Multinational Volunteer Army Federation Commanding Officer
Colonel Mikel</b>

06:42.960 --> 06:47.090
I am a political commissar 
and a lieutenant in the Federation Army.

06:47.450 --> 06:50.670
I'm just a flunky, you could say.

06:50.670 --> 06:55.050
I'll look up what "flunky" means 
in Federation language later.

06:55.320 --> 07:00.160
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Drake, 
with the Allied Kingdom's 42nd Aerial.

07:00.160 --> 07:02.990
We're glad to meet you, 
Lieutenant Colonel Drake.

07:02.990 --> 07:04.270
On behalf of the party,

07:04.270 --> 07:07.450
I give my deepest thanks to 
your unit's sacrifices and contributions.

07:07.920 --> 07:12.110
I'm sure my fallen comrades 
will appreciate that.

07:12.110 --> 07:13.010
Um...

07:14.320 --> 07:16.830
<b>Unified States Volunteer
Lt. Mary Sue</b>

07:14.330 --> 07:16.880
Are you a Federation Political Officer?

07:17.380 --> 07:18.780
Lieutenant Sue?

07:19.410 --> 07:21.910
I'm Lieutenant Mary Sue.

07:21.910 --> 07:26.720
I've heard that political officers 
give advice on aspects of military life.

07:27.040 --> 07:30.780
You see, our unit's fallen 
are buried in this land...

07:30.780 --> 07:33.180
Lieutenant, we discussed this.

07:33.450 --> 07:35.850
But they need to rest in their homeland!

07:36.290 --> 07:38.750
Please, allow them to be 
buried in their homelands.

07:39.680 --> 07:42.760
Everyone cares for their homeland.

07:42.760 --> 07:43.990
Right?

07:46.310 --> 07:49.440
I know exactly how you feel!

07:49.440 --> 07:52.780
If you'll let me, I'll help you 
in any way I can!

07:53.100 --> 07:55.040
R-Really?

07:56.510 --> 07:59.940
Lieutenant Sue, may I call you Mary?

07:59.940 --> 08:01.030
Of course!

08:01.030 --> 08:02.500
Thank you.

08:02.930 --> 08:05.040
Call me Liliya, too.

08:05.320 --> 08:08.020
Would you please be my friend?

08:08.020 --> 08:09.800
Yes, I'd love to.

08:10.750 --> 08:13.860
I'll help you prepare the memorandum.

08:13.860 --> 08:15.750
Yes, please do.

08:16.720 --> 08:20.320
Your lieutenant friend works fast.

08:21.130 --> 08:23.860
I'm sure you've got it tough, Colonel.

08:25.410 --> 08:28.880
She's better than most, actually.

08:29.550 --> 08:32.300
She is? You're joking.

08:34.210 --> 08:39.030
It's impossible to believe she's one 
of my country's political commissars.

08:39.310 --> 08:40.670
Well...

08:42.780 --> 08:44.040
I don't know what to say to that.

08:44.590 --> 08:46.850
But it's not good news.

08:57.900 --> 09:02.010
These harassment attacks 
get worse by the day.

09:02.360 --> 09:07.280
Why do the Federation soldiers go along 
with all these reckless attacks?

09:09.220 --> 09:11.780
What did the MP interrogators learn?

09:11.780 --> 09:14.240
The prisoners all said the same things.

09:14.640 --> 09:18.020
The sort of stuff you'd expect to hear 
from any communist sympathizer.

09:18.480 --> 09:20.740
I guess that's Commies for you.

09:20.740 --> 09:24.070
It looks like their 
"noble ideals" have spread

09:24.070 --> 09:26.450
throughout every inch of their territory.

09:26.450 --> 09:30.580
You really do hate communists, don't you?

09:31.000 --> 09:33.960
<i>I've been like that since my past life.</i>

09:33.960 --> 09:35.250
Um...

09:35.700 --> 09:38.950
I read the reports too.

09:38.950 --> 09:42.470
They all seem so identical, 
and filled with prejudice.

09:43.050 --> 09:44.640
What do you mean?

09:45.220 --> 09:48.850
I interviewed several of them myself.

09:48.850 --> 09:50.500
This is the report.

09:51.170 --> 09:52.840
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

09:52.840 --> 09:57.890
<i>the lieutenant's family fled 
the Federation during the revolution.</i>

09:57.890 --> 10:00.360
<i>It's good to have a living speaker 
of Federation language.</i>

10:02.740 --> 10:04.570
All of them except the political officers

10:04.570 --> 10:07.580
expressed a sentiment of 
estrangement from communism?

10:07.580 --> 10:08.380
Yes.

10:08.640 --> 10:13.540
More specifically, a lack of support 
for their superior officers.

10:13.540 --> 10:18.220
And it seemed like those voices 
were absent from the final reports...

10:24.300 --> 10:29.080
Officer, can I get a smoke?

10:29.480 --> 10:34.250
I'm an aerial mage. 
Regulations say I can't smoke.

10:35.790 --> 10:38.980
Tobacco ruins the lungs.

10:43.060 --> 10:45.620
No lighter then, either?

10:45.820 --> 10:48.000
Correct. My apologies.

10:48.690 --> 10:52.340
<i>Major Weiss is an old hand at this.</i>

10:55.020 --> 10:59.220
Tell me... Why do you people—no.

10:59.220 --> 11:01.080
Why do <i>you</i> fight?

11:01.340 --> 11:05.760
Why do we fight? We fight 
for ourselves, of course.

11:05.760 --> 11:08.100
We're fighting for a better future.

11:08.650 --> 11:10.100
A better future?

11:10.100 --> 11:15.310
If we beat you, our society 
will get a little better, right?

11:16.420 --> 11:17.910
Let me ask a different question.

11:18.220 --> 11:22.960
Why do you believe that fighting us 
will make your society better?

11:22.960 --> 11:24.920
Because you believe in communism?

11:25.890 --> 11:28.910
I believe in it about as much as you do.

11:30.430 --> 11:32.910
A very witty answer.

11:35.800 --> 11:38.240
Listen, you're an idiot, right?

11:39.280 --> 11:41.930
Is there anyone who doesn't 
love their homeland?

11:43.210 --> 11:44.920
Unconditionally.

11:45.590 --> 11:46.830
Am I wrong?

11:47.920 --> 11:52.370
Let me confirm. So you're fighting 
for your homeland, then?

11:54.010 --> 11:57.590
I heard that imperial soldiers were smart.

11:57.590 --> 12:01.180
But you're no better than 
the political commissars.

12:01.180 --> 12:02.420
Listen, you...

12:02.420 --> 12:04.240
We fight for our homeland.

12:04.240 --> 12:06.400
Do you need a reason beyond that?

12:06.400 --> 12:09.050
And if we can win 
some glory for ourselves,

12:09.050 --> 12:13.010
those fuckers in the party will 
actually listen to us for once.

12:23.750 --> 12:26.510
"Is there anyone who doesn't 
love their homeland?"

12:26.510 --> 12:28.210
That's what he said, right?

12:28.210 --> 12:29.760
Yes. Exactly those words.

12:30.700 --> 12:32.630
Fuck it all.

12:32.630 --> 12:35.170
That explains why their morale's 
so goddamn high...

12:35.540 --> 12:36.930
Lieutenant Colonel?

12:36.930 --> 12:37.760
Don't you get it?

12:38.300 --> 12:40.940
We thought we were fighting communists,

12:40.940 --> 12:43.230
but we've been fighting nationalists!

12:44.850 --> 12:49.620
<i>If anything, the way we're doing 
things now is making them stronger!</i>

12:57.750 --> 13:00.750
<b>Imperial Strategic HQ</b>

13:04.000 --> 13:06.880
I'll put this in simple terms, sir.

13:06.880 --> 13:09.170
We've killed too many of them.

13:09.900 --> 13:11.760
I'm surprised to hear you say that.

13:12.220 --> 13:14.150
I had thought a war like this one

13:14.150 --> 13:17.040
would be decided by who built 
the bigger pile of corpses.

13:17.040 --> 13:18.770
You're correct.

13:18.770 --> 13:23.440
But if we can defeat the enemy 
with words, not bullets...

13:23.440 --> 13:25.540
Words are far cheaper.

13:25.540 --> 13:28.150
But that's gotten us nowhere.

13:28.370 --> 13:33.150
We have saboteurs in the field conducting 
anti-communist propaganda efforts.

13:33.460 --> 13:36.470
And it's gotten us nowhere.

13:36.470 --> 13:38.040
Let's change our methods, then.

13:38.430 --> 13:41.790
Please throw ideological attacks 
into the garbage can.

13:42.670 --> 13:43.540
Excuse me?

13:43.540 --> 13:45.480
Logic isn't what we need.

13:45.480 --> 13:49.920
Sir, what's important is 
the emotions of the masses.

13:50.310 --> 13:55.370
Our propaganda efforts must 
not demoralize the enemy.

13:55.370 --> 13:57.560
Instead, we must work 
to split them apart.

13:58.320 --> 14:01.230
Our enemies aren't fighting 
out of loyalty to the party.

14:01.230 --> 14:04.370
They take up arms and 
fight for their homeland.

14:04.630 --> 14:07.610
Oh, the results of our 
interrogations are here.

14:08.980 --> 14:11.860
<i>Our MPs came into this with 
too many preconceived ideas.</i>

14:12.630 --> 14:15.890
<i>I hate the damn Commies myself,</i>

14:15.890 --> 14:18.370
<i>so I let myself be blinded, too.</i>

14:20.380 --> 14:25.120
It's not ideology that keeps our enemies 
in the fight, but nationalism.

14:25.120 --> 14:30.140
Which means we have to split the 
communists apart from everyone else.

14:30.140 --> 14:35.760
So we should "divide and conquer" in 
regard to the Federation's nationalism?

14:35.760 --> 14:40.630
No, "conquer" is something our military 
no longer has the strength to do.

14:40.820 --> 14:44.070
What we need is someone
 we can outsource the work to.

14:44.490 --> 14:46.780
A friend in need.

14:47.200 --> 14:49.420
An interesting proposal.

14:49.420 --> 14:54.240
But at my age, it's not easy 
to make new friends.

14:54.240 --> 14:58.260
But there's a famous diplomatic phrase.

14:58.260 --> 15:00.830
"The enemy of my enemy is my friend."

15:01.080 --> 15:04.080
Are you saying you have an idea 
as to who this friend could be?

15:04.370 --> 15:05.590
Of course.

15:06.180 --> 15:10.540
National councils in the occupied
regions on the Eastern front are ideal.

15:10.970 --> 15:13.050
If we work with them, we should be able

15:13.050 --> 15:15.670
to decrease the number of guerrilla 
attacks on the Eastern front.

15:17.430 --> 15:21.930
Sir, it's possible for us 
to make friends!

15:27.970 --> 15:29.860
We lost another supply truck?

15:29.860 --> 15:33.150
Yeah, it got attacked.

15:33.800 --> 15:37.000
We'll have to drink water 
to fill our bellies.

15:37.000 --> 15:40.870
I heard someone on one of the patrols 
died a suspicious death.

15:41.220 --> 15:44.540
And a story about the well 
being poisoned, too...

15:50.190 --> 15:51.600
Help yourself.

15:52.040 --> 15:54.720
What's wrong? What happened?

15:54.720 --> 15:57.750
N-Nothing...

15:57.750 --> 15:59.820
I'll say this just in case.

15:59.820 --> 16:04.050
You are to strictly obey international 
law when dealing with the locals.

16:04.050 --> 16:07.800
Even if something happens, 
deal with it appropriately.

16:07.800 --> 16:11.860
E-Even now, we have to treat them
 like we do when stationed back home?

16:11.860 --> 16:14.040
I'll be honest. We're at our limit.

16:14.500 --> 16:17.740
I understand how you feel, to a degree.

16:18.230 --> 16:21.490
But soon, you'll have 
nothing to worry about.

16:24.250 --> 16:26.750
<b>Federation Territory Imperial Occupation Area</b>

16:59.990 --> 17:03.540
Now, on behalf of the Empire,

17:03.540 --> 17:07.530
I, Lieutenant General Hans von Zettour, 
will give a speech.

17:08.470 --> 17:11.310
I say to all of you listening to this...

17:11.310 --> 17:15.360
that we, the Empire, want one thing.

17:16.260 --> 17:17.530
Peace.

17:17.530 --> 17:24.310
I want peace for my homeland, 
just as do you all.

17:25.820 --> 17:28.310
Peace, peace, peace.

17:28.840 --> 17:32.130
If it weren't for those 
accursed communists,

17:32.130 --> 17:37.410
would we have taken up arms? 
Would you have?

17:37.820 --> 17:42.580
<i>We have simply taken up the sword 
to defend our homeland.</i>

17:42.870 --> 17:46.580
<i>We promise that when peace is achieved,</i>

17:46.580 --> 17:50.340
<i>we will lay down our arms and 
return to our beloved homeland.</i>

17:50.340 --> 17:55.080
<i>We have no intention of 
absorbing territories we occupy.</i>

17:55.080 --> 17:59.580
<i>Our greatest desire is to co-exist 
with independent peoples</i>

17:59.580 --> 18:02.430
<i>who have their own territories 
and governments!</i>

18:03.230 --> 18:06.840
Is there anyone who doesn't 
love their homeland?

18:06.840 --> 18:10.240
Is there anyone who 
doesn't love their home?

18:10.240 --> 18:11.860
We beg you...

18:12.400 --> 18:15.350
As good friends,

18:16.090 --> 18:19.080
like Horatius at the Bridge,

18:19.080 --> 18:23.530
please allow us to walk alongside you!

18:24.320 --> 18:27.240
<i>Truly, a wonderful person 
as an individual,</i>

18:27.240 --> 18:29.770
<i>and a monster as part of an organization.</i>

18:30.410 --> 18:35.430
On behalf of the Empire, 
I announce today...

18:41.540 --> 18:46.250
that we will turn our military-controlled 
areas over to civilian rule!

18:53.290 --> 18:58.230
May light shine on 
the future of the Reich,

18:58.530 --> 19:00.700
and its good friends!

19:02.340 --> 19:05.740
<i>What a con artist.</i>

19:06.140 --> 19:11.410
<i>I'm sure he's got a special room 
waiting for him in hell.</i>

19:13.880 --> 19:16.630
<b>Allied Kingdom Embassy in Moskva</b>

19:14.200 --> 19:17.040
To new friends!

19:17.040 --> 19:20.140
To glorious cooperation 
between our two armies!

19:20.140 --> 19:22.730
We'd love to open a second front,

19:22.730 --> 19:25.220
so that we can show the Empire 
what good friends we are!

19:25.220 --> 19:30.470
Of course. But our homeland is in 
the midst of a vast air war...

19:31.580 --> 19:34.980
Comrade Secretary, we have a problem!

19:34.980 --> 19:37.600
The Empire... has joined forces!

19:37.600 --> 19:40.980
They've joined forces with 
the ethno-nationalists!

19:40.980 --> 19:45.080
They've started the process of 
creating temporary governments

19:45.080 --> 19:47.970
and transferring power 
within their territories!

19:49.200 --> 19:51.240
The enemy of the world...

19:51.240 --> 19:54.590
The Empire... has made friends!

19:59.960 --> 20:05.090
<i>Thanks to him, the Empire 
may live to see another day.</i>

20:10.580 --> 20:14.900
<i>Now, if only we had a friend who was 
more useful at ending the war...</i>

20:14.900 --> 20:16.340
Oh, Lieutenant Colonel!

20:16.340 --> 20:19.440
There was coffee on the resupply list!

20:19.980 --> 20:21.690
What? Really?

20:21.690 --> 20:24.350
Yes. The lowest grade 
of the stuff, though.

20:24.350 --> 20:26.690
I won't ask for much in 
these circumstances!

20:26.950 --> 20:29.200
Caffeine!

20:30.510 --> 20:32.630
Mehr Licht, as they say.

20:32.630 --> 20:35.080
Allow me to prepare you some coffee...

20:35.080 --> 20:38.300
Black as the devil, 
hot as hell, pure as an angel,

20:38.300 --> 20:41.390
and sweet as love!

20:43.360 --> 20:45.220
Thanks.

20:48.970 --> 20:53.400
<i>Thinking back, this was all thanks 
to my talented second officer.</i>

20:53.630 --> 20:56.380
<i>I've known her since 
the battles of the Rhine,</i>

20:56.380 --> 20:59.400
<i>but it feels presumptuous to 
even call her a mere friend now.</i>

21:00.080 --> 21:03.570
<i>Who else have I known that long?</i>

21:05.840 --> 21:09.010
<i>Not you! Fuck you!</i>

21:09.010 --> 21:12.010
Lieutenant, what is that 
damn doll doing here?

21:12.010 --> 21:14.330
It was in a home we occupied.

21:14.330 --> 21:15.790
I thought it was cute.

21:15.790 --> 21:16.620
Throw it out!

21:16.620 --> 21:18.930
Throw it out this instant!

21:20.130 --> 21:23.130
<b>Ildoa Kingdom Army Command</b>

21:23.360 --> 21:27.130
They've set up national councils for 
self-rule in Federation territory?

21:27.130 --> 21:31.140
Our allies are big believers 
in Raison d'État, I see.

21:31.430 --> 21:37.440
I hope they're as willing to listen to us,
 since we're their friends as well.

23:11.620 --> 23:16.350
Um, why don't you attend 
the prisoners' interrogations, too?

23:16.350 --> 23:17.930
I'm surprised.

23:17.930 --> 23:19.750
As long as you've been here, 
you're still saying that?

23:20.040 --> 23:21.940
Look at me.

23:22.740 --> 23:25.050
Look at me!

23:25.050 --> 23:27.140
They'll think I'm just a little kid!

23:27.140 --> 23:29.400
Am I supposed to look up at them 
during the whole interrogation?

23:29.400 --> 23:31.700
It'll look like I'm a lost kid 
at the police station!

23:31.700 --> 23:33.470
A-Apologies!

23:33.470 --> 23:35.630
I'll get a kid's high chair, then!

23:35.630 --> 23:37.560
No!

23:35.640 --> 23:40.090
<b>Next Time
Well-Intentioned Mediator</b>
